  "question": {
    "text": "The equation of state of a real gas is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>V</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> are pressure, volume and temperature respectively and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is the universal gas constant. The dimensions of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math> is similar to that of :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>V</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mpadded><mi>R</mi></mpadded></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>From the dimensional analysis, it follows that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi>PV</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>And,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>]</mo></math></p><p>Hence,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mfenced></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi>PV</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p>"
  }
}